    {
      "id": "f48328b0-54d8-419a-8750-7357ccdc24bc",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        928,
        10544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 992,
        "content": "## Monitor Amazon wish list prices with Apify and alert on drops via Telegram\n\n### Who's it for\n\nShoppers and deal hunters who want one price tracker for every Amazon item they care about, without paying a third-party monitoring subscription. You keep the list in a Google Sheet, and Telegram pings you when a price crosses your target.\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a schedule, reads Amazon wish list items from Google Sheets, and uses an Apify actor to fetch current product pricing. It updates the sheet with the latest scraped data and checks whether a price-drop condition is met. When an item qualifies, it sends a Telegram text alert.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Schedule Trigger with the desired checking frequency.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the spreadsheet/range containing the Amazon item URLs, stored prices, and alert criteria.\n- Configure the Apify credentials and actor input so it can scrape the Amazon product or wish list data from each sheet row.\n- Set the If node condition to match your price-drop rule, such as current price below target price or below the previous recorded price.\n- Connect Telegram bot credentials and set the target chat ID/message template for alerts.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the sheet columns, Apify actor parameters, price-drop threshold, and Telegram message text to match how you track wishlist items.\nSwap the Amazon Product Scraper for another Apify Actor to track flights, real estate, Steam games, or crypto, and replace Telegram with Slack or email."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
